WEBVTT

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:36.570
After-School Pleiades

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:42.740
Sobbingly, I went on my journey

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:47.210
Wishing I could at least fly through the sky

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:53.590
And yet the stars gently shone on me in the nights after our quarrels

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:59.140
I wonder if you were also watching them

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:04.390
I don't know... I want to know... I want to feel it...

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:11.440
Nothingness simply means there are infinite possibilities

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:15.230
The excitement I got after realizing that

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:18.320
was like surfing the waves of space and time

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:23.410
How strange that I'm not afraid anymore

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:26.120
Let's embrace our imperfections and go on

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:29.000
We'll open the promised door

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:34.170
and gain dazzling smiles!

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:56.400
Which was that?

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:57.360
Mi.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:00.740
And that?

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:02.280
Ti, Re, and Do.

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:03.910
Then this?

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:06.910
All but Sol.

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:13.880
Dream of Sol

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:18.880
Yes, that's the only key that makes no sound.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:19.630
Terrible.

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:22.840
Incredible! You can tell what
notes they are just by ear?

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:23.930
She has perfect pitch!

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:25.680
It's nothing that impressive.

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:28.350
It only means I get to be Nanako's toy.

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:31.520
Well, I'm off to the library.

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:35.060
Huh? Isn't that the book
you borrowed yesterday?

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:36.360
Did you finish it already?

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:37.400
Y-Yeah.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.030
Hikaru never finishes a book.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:39.610
Huh?

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:41.700
Her bookmark is still where she first placed it.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:42.860
I'm surprised you noticed.

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:44.120
You're always that way.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:45.910
You never finish watching movies, either.

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:47.030
Or even music.

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:49.660
By the time I'm halfway through,
I understand most of it.

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:51.290
If I already get it, isn't that enough?

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:53.830
Then there's no point in reading in the first place.

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:56.420
That's not true. There are good books out there.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:58.000
I don't get it.

00:03:58.340 --> 00:03:59.920
There is this, too.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:00.380
Concert Beneath the Starry Sky

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:00.380
Sending a message to Cetus's Gliese

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:02.340
Where did you get that?

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:08.720
Concert Beneath the Starry Sky

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:08.720
"Concert Beneath the Starry Sky,
Sending a Message to Cetus's Gliese..."

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:10.430
A piano concert in the observatory?

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:13.190
They're trying to send piano music into space.

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:14.440
Huh? When?

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:16.190
Next week, every night for the whole week.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:17.610
What about it?

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:19.940
Hikaru's mother is the observatory head.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:20.820
Really?

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:22.360
The pianist is her father.

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:29.160
The meteor shower forecast...

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:36.380
There!

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:37.840
What a convenient alien.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.840
But that just looks like the Moon.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:44.680
H-Huh? That can't be right.

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:50.470
Prepping for tomorrow
(home late)

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:50.470
Father

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:50.470
Ditto

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:50.470
School -> Club

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:50.470
Hikaru,
There's salad in the fridge.
Warm up the stew on the stove
and have some.
- Mom

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:07.320
I knew it! I wasn't wrong!

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:08.910
Look at this!

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.200
The next fragment

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.710
is trapped in orbit around the Moon.

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:18.460
"The Moon" Moon?

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:21.090
What's the problem? Let's go to the Moon.

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:23.130
Hold on, we're talking about the Moon!

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:24.340
"The Moon" Moon.

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:26.680
Well, we did go to space the other day.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:29.100
That was only an altitude of 400km!

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:30.350
It was still part of Earth!

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:33.390
Hey, don't you want to fix your spaceship?

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:34.680
Well, of course.

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:36.810
Do you have anyone else you can rely on?

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:38.400
If I did, I'd have no trouble.

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:41.020
Then we don't have any choice but to go.

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:42.280
I see...

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:44.400
You're doing it for us.

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:48.160
Well, no one's ever done this before, right?

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:49.160
It sounds like fun.

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:49.990
Huh?

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:52.410
Then it's time for training!

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:59.380
Surrender yourself to gravity
until you count to a hundred!

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:00.380
You can't be serious!

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:01.920
Now accelerate!

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:03.800
Ninety degrees to perpendicular fall!

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:05.130
From here?

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:09.930
Just to get to Earth's orbit,
you must reach at least Mach 7.

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:12.510
To reach the Moon, you need four more Machs!

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:14.100
Mach is for speed of sound, isn't it?

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:17.480
However, at that speed,
it'll take three full days one way.

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:19.350
You mean we need to fly even faster than that?

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:20.400
Of course!

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.440
I cannot force you girls to skip school.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:24.900
I'm getting worried now.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:26.030
Now climb!

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:27.780
Pull up at once!

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:31.740
See you later!

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.080
The air's heavy...

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:42.210
Wait, Hikaru!

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:45.090
Why? This is easy.

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:47.550
No, it isn't!

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:50.180
It looks like we'll have a good wind tomorrow,

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:54.260
so let's try to recover the fragment
then, Thursday, after school.

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:54.970
Wind?

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:56.680
That's sooner than I expected.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:57.560
Tomorrow?

00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:58.890
What's wrong, Subaru?

00:06:59.890 --> 00:06:59.980
Concert Beneath the Starry Sky

00:06:59.890 --> 00:06:59.980
Sending a message to Cetus's Gliese

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:01.600
The concert.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:04.770
I was planning to go tomorrow...

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:06.400
Hikaru, have you already been?

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:07.150
I'm not going.

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:07.610
Huh?

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:08.990
Let's go together, then!

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:12.240
Besides, they aren't holding it tomorrow, anyway.

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:13.570
Huh?

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:17.580
You're right. Why are they skipping that day?

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:20.870
What do they mean by sending a song into space?

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:24.960
They discovered a planet similar to Earth
in Cetus's Gliese planetary system.

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:26.460
Oh?

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:29.170
So they're sending piano music toward it

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:33.720
to say, "Hello, we're here,"
to anyone that might be living there.

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:35.350
That's romantic.

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:37.010
You all don't need to do that.

00:07:37.010 --> 00:07:40.390
You have an extraterrestrial life
form right here, don't you?

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:43.060
I've kind of lost interest.

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:44.190
What?

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:49.780
No one really thinks it'll reach
any extraterrestrial life forms.

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:54.660
Even if the music we send reaches that far,
it'll take centuries to arrive.

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:57.660
We don't even know if anyone is out there.

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:04.670
In other words, this concert's real goal is to make the observatory a topic of discussion among Earthlings.

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:06.710
Huh...

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:09.510
Concert Beneath the Starry Sky

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:09.510
Sending a message to Cetus's Gliese

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:17.810
Hey.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:23.310
Huh? I meant to go back to my classroom
to pick up something I forgot...

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:24.560
Really?

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:26.310
Did something happen?

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:28.690
You have that look again.

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:29.570
Huh?

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:34.570
There are always just buds here,

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:38.200
but I bet when the flowers bloom,
it'll be really pretty.

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:40.080
The flowers here won't bloom.

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:42.580
They mustn't bloom.

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:45.580
Why not? Will they be buds forever?

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:48.590
If flowers bloom at the wrong time,

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:52.090
they will wither, without ever bearing fruit.

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:56.340
But I bet they'd be pretty.

00:08:58.550 --> 00:09:01.180
Do you think it's all right not
to watch them bloom

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:03.850
if you know what kind of flower they'll become?

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:07.350
You don't know what flowers
will bloom until they do.

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:11.230
Who are you actually referring to?

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:13.650
A friend.

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:16.410
You're a kind person.

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:17.740
Why?

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:19.240
You take them at their word.

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:20.740
Hikaru...

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:24.000
wouldn't lie.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:28.000
Subaru, are you able to express
your feelings directly in words?

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:29.630
No.

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:34.050
Everyone has a door that they've
locked before even they realize it.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:38.220
Minato, the way you express
things is always so complicated.

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:38.840
Is it?

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:40.010
It is!

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:41.010
You think so?

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:45.770
If I told you I was going to the Moon,
would you believe me?

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:46.600
Yeah.

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:48.600
Really?

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:52.070
Do you have some reason to lie to me?

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:05.870
A fragment captured by the Moon, huh?

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:11.340
Mother

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:11.340
Home late
(might be out overnight)

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:11.340
Afternoon
wake-up -> work
(at home)

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:11.340
Hikaru

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:11.090
Father...

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:13.630
He's here today.

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:14.840
That's unusual.

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:36.070
School -> Moon!

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:49.080
Now, everyone, let's go!

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:50.830
Unfurl the sails.

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:51.630
Sails?

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:53.920
Widen our magic circle!

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:55.130
Like this?

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:55.920
Farther!

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:57.170
Wider and wider!

00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:58.920
Can this really get us to the Moon?

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:01.090
We caught the wind!

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:02.390
Th-The wind?

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:06.220
We're riding the shock wave born of contact
between Earth's geomagnetism

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:07.850
and a solar wind!

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:10.730
There's wind on the sun?

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:13.360
It's the spring constellations.

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:26.620
I'm sorry. There's a problem with the
equipment, so I'll be staying overnight.

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:29.040
You should rest, in preparation for tomorrow.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:30.500
Has Hikaru come home?

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:32.000
ool -> Moon!

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:33.330
The Moon?

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:35.040
What does that mean?

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:38.510
I see...

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:42.840
You should come over right now, then.

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:46.510
No, I don't mean for work. After all,

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:50.810
has that girl ever lied to us before?

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:56.730
I hear different sounds than usual.

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:59.320
That's because we're away from noisy Earth.

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:01.280
Though it's still too early to lower our guards.

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:05.570
You can pick up radio waves?

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:07.240
Some signals are crossed, that's all.

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:09.290
Would you all like to try?

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:11.370
No, we'll pass.

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:15.210
I'm happy enough just seeing this.

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:17.380
This is the actual Moon...

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:19.840
I didn't know it was so easy.

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:21.880
I-It isn't easy at all!

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:25.720
With rockets, it takes several days to get here!

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:27.970
The front and back of the Moon have
different geological features,

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:29.350
and there are lots of things we don't know—

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:30.600
What's wrong, Subaru?

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:32.600
Anyway, it's incredible!

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:34.650
This is amazing! It isn't boring at—

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:35.900
There's something shining.

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:36.650
It's the fragment!

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:37.820
Wait, behind us!

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:41.780
That Horned Cape appeared again?

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:43.700
Why do you always show up?

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:45.950
Because the stars led me here.

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:52.750
Why do you always stand in my way?

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:55.540
M-Maybe I'm being led by something, too.

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:56.920
I hate jokes!

00:12:57.170 --> 00:12:59.290
Then I'll lead you!

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:00.380
There!

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:05.970
Subaru, are you all right?

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:08.680
Huh? Subaru?

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:11.560
Aoi!

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:13.060
Ow!

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:14.390
Whoa, there...

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:16.100
Thank you.

00:13:16.100 --> 00:13:18.520
Ah, the magic circle is breaking up!

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:21.230
Everyone, brace for impact!

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:25.360
Subaru!

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:26.450
Hikaru!

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:34.910
Huh? This is...

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:37.920
Those are stars?

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:43.210
And that's Earth? Meaning this is...

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:43.920
No way...

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:48.640
Incredible! Hikaru, we're on the Moon!

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:52.680
I'm sorry to interrupt your fun, but this is a dream.

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:54.060
Probably mine.

00:13:56.230 --> 00:14:02.070
Which would mean you're a Subaru
created by my subconscious.

00:13:56.560 --> 00:13:58.770
It's bouncy!

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:04.030
This is incredible, Hikaru!

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:06.740
The Moon looks delicious!

00:14:10.070 --> 00:14:11.120
She ate it.

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:13.330
I'm sorry, Subarun...

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:17.500
It looks like my subconscious doesn't think too highly of your intellectuality.

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:22.500
Why am I having this dream?

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:26.880
I feel like I need to wake up soon, but...

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:28.510
Hikaru.

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:30.220
It's delicious.

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:36.770
You're right.

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:41.150
I can't remember where it's from,
but it tastes sweet and familiar.

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:42.820
See?

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:49.860
Hikaru, how were you
able to become a magic user?

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:52.030
You can do everything, and you know everything.

00:14:52.030 --> 00:14:54.410
You're the complete opposite of me.

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:59.410
That just means you have the
wrong image of me, Subarun.

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:06.130
Even if I try to talk like I'm better,
I can only do things partway.

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:13.510
I don't even have the courage to finish
listening to my father's song to the end...

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:18.640
Just like our president said,
I'm a bigger nobody than everyone else.

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:20.270
I'm more than qualified.

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:22.270
Your father's song?

00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:23.730
Look.

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:28.070
That's it. Dreams are rather convenient like that.

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:30.570
That's your father's song?

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:32.910
Yes, I remember seeing it.

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:34.620
But...

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:38.290
Ah, no, I can't!

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:39.870
Why not? Don't you want to hear it?

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:42.290
That's enough! Hurry up and wake up, self!

00:15:44.710 --> 00:15:47.050
Hikaru, you're awake!

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:49.300
Subarun, this song...

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:52.050
Yes, we've been hearing it this whole time.

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:54.340
This isn't a dream?

00:15:54.340 --> 00:15:55.550
Why can I hear it?

00:15:56.430 --> 00:15:58.720
It's coming from Earth...

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:03.060
But the concert isn't happening tonight.

00:16:04.310 --> 00:16:05.610
That's right.

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:08.440
The Moon is blocking Gliese tonight, so...

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:10.360
The Moon...

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:18.290
Do you think maybe your mother and father
know that you're here, on the Moon?

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:20.950
What are you saying? Of course they don't.

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:22.250
How could they...

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:24.290
You're right.

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:25.710
-> Moon!

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:28.750
I wrote "Moon" on our whiteboard at home...

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:29.630
Huh?

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:30.630
Then they really...

00:16:30.630 --> 00:16:32.050
They'd really play because of that?

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:33.880
Yes, that must be it!

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:36.640
Wait, how do you know
about my father, Subarun?

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:39.060
Huh? Weren't we just talking about him?

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:40.810
Even our dreams are getting crossed?

00:16:40.810 --> 00:16:42.640
I swear, up here, anything goes!

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:47.560
That day, I was in bed with a fever.

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:52.530
I could hear the sound of a piano
coming from Father's room.

00:16:53.740 --> 00:17:01.160
But at the time, the piano tone sounded
like it was troubled over something.

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:05.750
And then, I could see the note.

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:09.750
I knew that was the note
my father was searching for.

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:14.340
I couldn't understand why I did that.

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:15.840
But...

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:18.100
I was afraid.

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:23.930
I worried that the measure I wrote
would cause trouble for my father.

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:27.310
Once I started thinking that,
I grew so afraid, I couldn't bear it.

00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:34.110
I could never listen to that song to the end.

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:45.500
My father and mother both achieved
their dreams on their own.

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:50.040
I just didn't want to interfere with them.

00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:01.560
Subaru, Hikaru, can you hear it?

00:18:01.560 --> 00:18:02.930
Yeah, I can hear it.

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:04.100
Yeah, we're all right.

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:05.520
Let's keep going like this.

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:07.480
We'll trap the fragment from two sides.

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:08.650
That's direct.

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:10.110
Simple is good.

00:18:12.110 --> 00:18:15.110
There's Nanako's team's magic
circle. They're working fast...

00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:17.570
We're really on the Moon.

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:18.530
Yeah.

00:18:19.110 --> 00:18:20.620
Hey, Hikaru?

00:18:21.280 --> 00:18:23.700
You don't need to worry about me.

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:27.000
I wouldn't give up on using magic
just because we went to the Moon.

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:28.120
Right?

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:31.670
Yeah, but you're half wrong.

00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:33.840
You weren't interfering.

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:34.460
Huh?

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:37.050
What you did as a child.

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:40.470
That's why he's playing it like
this, to let you hear it.

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:42.350
You don't know that.

00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:44.970
You don't want to hear how your father feels?

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:49.810
That's right. I'm scared to find out...

00:18:52.310 --> 00:18:53.230
It's him!

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:54.230
Huh?

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:56.820
That guy's so easy to read!

00:18:56.820 --> 00:18:57.610
Let's go!

00:18:57.610 --> 00:18:58.700
Yeah!

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:01.660
What?

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:03.660
Huh? We connected with him?

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:04.660
How?

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:06.580
Are you planning to use me?

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:08.870
I guess this makes it a convenient three-on-three.

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:10.120
Let's do it like this!

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:12.460
Then I'll use you all, as well!

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:14.340
Everyone, brace for impact!

00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:14.960
Again?

00:19:25.510 --> 00:19:27.850
<i>I can't listen to the end of it.</i>

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:32.850
<i>Because I know that once
I hear it, I'll have to cry.</i>

00:19:33.810 --> 00:19:37.860
<i>But I don't want anyone to see me like that.</i>

00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:41.200
Subarun...

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:45.200
The Moon was delicious, wasn't it?

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:46.660
Yeah.

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:11.560
What do you think? Did it reach?

00:20:11.980 --> 00:20:14.900
Yes, perfectly. It's all fixed.

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:15.730
Thank you.

00:20:16.310 --> 00:20:18.400
That was a lovely performance, thanks to you.

00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:20.820
We wanted our daughter to hear it.

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:29.790
It's true that Hikaru has never lied to us.

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:32.710
She's a better daughter than we deserve.

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:36.590
We've been completely
spoiled by her, haven't we?

00:20:37.340 --> 00:20:39.420
Let's invite her tomorrow.

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:43.090
Sure. But do you think she'll come?

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:46.760
Tomorrow, let's ask her together.

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:53.350
Huh? Is this our clubroom?

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:56.650
But weren't we just on the Moon?

00:20:56.650 --> 00:20:57.810
Amazing.

00:20:57.810 --> 00:20:58.690
Hikaru?

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:00.400
Huh?

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:04.530
I get it!

00:21:04.530 --> 00:21:06.360
When we stabilized the fragment,

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:09.370
it started resonating with the other
fragments we have in this room and—

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:12.700
There are tears in your eyes.

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:14.660
What's wrong? Did something happen?

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:17.290
It's nothing! Jerk! Don't look!

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:18.840
Did he do something?

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:21.130
No, it wasn't him.

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:23.800
Oh, but I wonder what happened to him...

00:21:24.130 --> 00:21:27.510
Nothing would happen to him! I'm sure
he'll appear again before we know it!

00:21:27.840 --> 00:21:29.100
Don't get off-topic.

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:30.350
What do you mean, "off-topic"?

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:33.730
We just went to the Moon
and captured a fragment.

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:36.190
Could there be anything more amazing?

00:21:36.190 --> 00:21:37.730
That is overwhelming, is it not?

00:21:37.730 --> 00:21:40.610
There aren't many things that
can make one cry from joy.

00:21:47.200 --> 00:21:50.080
To Be Continued

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:48.780
What?!

00:21:57.250 --> 00:22:01.710
You see, when I looked up

00:22:01.710 --> 00:22:07.090
everyone was smiling at me

00:22:07.090 --> 00:22:16.810
both embarrassed and happy as the starry sky turned sideways

00:22:16.810 --> 00:22:25.780
Ever since then, whenever my daily life seemed hopeless

00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:23.150
...my daily life...

00:22:25.780 --> 00:22:35.540
I'd go into myself just for a little bit and ask

00:22:35.540 --> 00:22:37.410
"Can I fly?"

00:22:37.410 --> 00:22:41.630
"Sky" shall be our meeting point

00:22:41.630 --> 00:22:47.260
We can go there whenever we want to

00:22:47.260 --> 00:22:56.930
The wind sows stars in the far distance only light leaps to

00:22:56.930 --> 00:23:01.560
"We have to catch them!"

00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:06.070
In the very moment I reached out my hand,

00:23:06.070 --> 00:23:11.410
the scenery around us glittered

00:23:11.660 --> 00:23:16.120
sometime after school

00:23:20.500 --> 00:23:24.290
Just as the Moon orbits Earth, there are many
satellites orbiting other planets, as well!

00:23:24.710 --> 00:23:26.090
Pluto has Charon.

00:23:26.090 --> 00:23:27.090
Macaron?

00:23:27.090 --> 00:23:27.960
Jupiter has Kale.

00:23:27.960 --> 00:23:28.720
Curry?

00:23:28.720 --> 00:23:29.720
Saturn has...

00:23:29.720 --> 00:23:32.180
Next episode:
A Hat, Ice, and a Princess.

00:23:32.180 --> 00:23:33.090
Pan.

00:23:33.090 --> 00:23:35.010
I'm hungry!
